Tywelwyn is a 6'11" deerfolk, with dappled brown fur and tall, branching antlers. His muscles are far larger than could be achieved without magical or chemical intervention, and his skin is hot enough that his sweat sizzles as it's produced.

He is the founder and leader of the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]], a protection racket in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]. He was rumored to have gone crazy, hearing voices, but it appears that he's struck a deal with someone in [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]]. Formerly unable to wield magic, he now pilots a simulacrum to work on his behalf. A journal taken from [[Benjamin Grayson]]'s private study complains that "that idiot deer" is two-timing him by having his people set up radar dishes after an agreement, and the Party took this to mean Tywelwyn.

He did not leave his room in the basement of 412 Anchor Boulevard in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]]; he sent out simulacra instead, made by a magic item he had to stay near.

What the Party found in the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] was not the deerfolk they had met. It was a burnt-out husk: a tall humanoid shape of black, solidified matter, hollow, with flame burning where its chest and skull had been and two black-stained antlers still on its head. It wore a raiment of jet black, where his simulacrum had worn the raiment of the Host, and it was mobile and alight.

He was no werecreature, unlike the Roundhats around him. He threw fire and divine lances, and a black cape fought at his shoulder. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] killed him by making his own mind drive a body that could not move, and it tore itself apart.

He made the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/An Iron Gauntlet in a Glass Glove|Heart]] in the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]], using a recipe that [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] gave him, and the fane's deeper rooms and six god doors were built around it. He used the chunk of obsidian at the fane's center to make his simulacra, and, because a Heart cannot be moved on its own, fed it that rock as a power source to shift it from the tavern where it was made.

His office behind the War door held a typewriter and chalkboards: a map of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] with points circled, and sheet music and harmonies pointing at the same points. His notes are about resonance, vibrating one thing to make another answer at the same frequency, and work out a scheme to spread a particular harmony through Hallia with radar dishes so the city vibrates at the same frequency as something far away and lets it come to Hallia. He did not have the full picture; parts of the notes are only question marks. He was preparing a pilgrimage behind the Giant door, and the [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] is for Pyre.

His ledgers show the Roundhats skimming from the Gas-n-Go and two other franchises, the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]], two laundromats, a churro restaurant and a fried chicken restaurant.
